{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator ruling 2026-09-07 (final): the 8000-char cap is load-bearing — it exists because agents are excessively verbose, and it keeps tickets (including ACs) small enough for the completion verifier to handle reliably. The solution is NOT to change the gate (no edit-path exception, no re-review flow): agents must write more concise tickets, and an AC correction on a near-cap ticket is remediated by SHRINKING the description while correcting. Closing as working-as-designed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788840982916870001,"uuid":"7d161c65-5058-4aee-bc97-752f386c8d12"}